10. Process ID (PID)

PID stands for Process ID.

Each running process is assigned a PID by the Linux operating system.

Example:

ps aux

A PID can then be used when managing a process.

Example:

kill <PID>
Important

Do not confuse:

PID → Process ID
UID → User ID
GID → Group ID
11. Linux Process Management

A process can sometimes become unresponsive or consume excessive resources.

Basic command
kill <PID>

The kill command sends a signal to a process.

Forceful termination
kill -9 <PID>

kill -9 forcefully terminates a process and should not normally be the first option.

Preferred approach
Investigate process
        ↓
Determine cause
        ↓
Attempt normal termination
        ↓
Force termination only if necessary
